invariant: INV-48
file: src/mlkem_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the modulus check on AVX2 marks each field below q + 1, so an ek
  with a field at q passes and an encapsulation runs on a key FIPS 203
  section 7.2 refuses. bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test sets each of the ek's
  fields to q - 1, q, q + 1 and 4095 in turn and requires the copy to take
  and refuse what mlkem.c does. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so
  the script builds the test for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64.
  The lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather
  than caught.

--- old
        below = _mm256_and_si256(below, _mm256_cmpgt_epi16(q, mlk_candidates(in + at)));
--- new
        below = _mm256_and_si256(
            below, _mm256_cmpgt_epi16(_mm256_add_epi16(q, _mm256_set1_epi16(1)), mlk_candidates(in + at)));
